# Hand-authored clump stamps: one folder per source, each holding a diffuse
# (sRGB, alpha carries the cutout), an arm and a 16-bit disp map. One whole tuft
# per stamp, standing the way it is drawn with its base on the bottom edge —
# unlike a leaf stamp, nothing here is ever rotated, so the stamp is the cell.
# `source.json` declares heightMetres. No normal map — scatter-forge derives it
# from the height. See ../../../../docs/scatter-forge.md.
#
# Large binaries, kept out of git the way /assets/ is. With no source here the
# forge generates its blades instead, so a fresh clone still builds. This rule
# keeps the file itself tracked so the folder survives that clone.
*
!.gitignore
